  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "#Introduction to a Filter & Sort Pipeline\r\n\r\n**Goal**: Act as the \"algorithm\" to curate a video feed. You will process a set of MyTube video cards using two different pipelines to see how the order of operations affects efficiency and fairness.\r\n\r\n####**Part 1: Filter First**\r\n\r\n* *Filter*: Keep only cards with the \"Sports\" tag.\r\n\r\n* *Sort*: Order them by Score (High to Low). **Scoring Rule**: *Score = Likes − Dislikes + Subscribers*\r\n\r\n* *Rank*: Place the top 2 in the Rank Slots.\r\n\r\n####**Part 2: Sort First**\r\n\r\n* *Reset*: Clear the board.\r\n\r\n* *Sort*: Order ALL cards by Score (High to Low).  **Scoring Rule**: *Score = Likes − Dislikes + Subscribers*\r\n\r\n* *Filter*: Select the first 2 cards from the top that have the \"Sports\" tag.\r\n\r\n* *Rank*: Place them in the Rank Slots.\r\n\r\n",
